        "AnswerCount": "0",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;Related to &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.meta.stackexchange.com/q/303/4762&quot;&gt;Do we have Standardised Comments?&lt;/a&gt;, I happened to stumble upon this link on Github, &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Benjol&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Benjol&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Benjol/SE-AutoReviewComments&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;SE-AutoReviewComments&lt;/a&gt;, whilst reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://meta.askubuntu.com/questions/19503/is-it-acceptable-to-copy-other-users-common-moderation-related-comments?cb=1#comment42187_19504&quot;&gt;this comment&lt;/a&gt; from this question on AskUbuntu's meta site, &lt;a href=&quot;https://meta.askubuntu.com/q/19503/348964&quot;&gt;Is it acceptable to copy other user's common, moderation-related comments?&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As yet, I am not sure how useful it would be or what we could do with it, but I thought I'd just make it known, if anyone has any ideas (i.e. cloning it for our use; making our own Github (or Gitlab) repository for ours, or; whatever) then post them below.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr /&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;It turns out that Paulster2 mentioned it in &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.meta.stackexchange.com/a/315/4762&quot;&gt;an answer&lt;/a&gt; to &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.meta.stackexchange.com/q/303/4762&quot;&gt;Do we have Standardised Comments?&lt;/a&gt;, so I haven't discovered anything new, after all.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2021-02-21T09:29:40.710",
