        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AcceptedAnswerId": "484",
        "AnswerCount": "1",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;So, recently I was looking at an answer, I clicked on the vote up button because it was good and then noticed I already had. The score changed to 2 and I un vote-upped it. Is this supposed to happen? The answer is &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/11580/xyz-davinci-3d-printer-constantly-jamming?answertab=oldest#tab-top&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2020-04-19T03:24:29.057",
        "Id": "483",
        "LastActivityDate": "2020-04-19T05:47:54.840",
        "OwnerUserId": "19482",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "5",
        "Tags": "&lt;bug&gt;&lt;down-votes&gt;&lt;up-votes&gt;",
        "Title": "Am I supposed to be able to vote up twice?",
        "ViewCount": "48"
      },
      {
