        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "1",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;The tag &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/tags/flashforge-adventure-3/info&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;flashforge-adventure-3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was created due to a mis-spelled tag in a question which has since been corrected. Can this tag be deleted?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;(bad) Alternatively, can it be added as a synonym for the &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/tags/flashforge-adventurer-3/info&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;flashforge-adventurer-3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (the correct tag has an extra &lt;code&gt;r&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Lastly, As I (thankfully) don't have access to the mod tools, can someone with access do the needful?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "1",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2018-10-23T12:27:06.843",
