      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "0",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;Many people find it's hard to get a good guide for 3d printing.  Is a question about what printer a beginner should get on topic?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "ClosedDate": "2016-01-31T18:17:49.480",
        "CommentCount": "3",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-31T14:36:08.830",
        "Id": "88",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-01-31T14:36:08.830",
        "OwnerUserId": "219",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "0",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;&lt;7-questions&gt;",
        "Title": "Are questions about 3d printer reccomendations on or off topic?",
        "ViewCount": "18"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "2",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I feel like questions along the lines of, &quot;my printer is crashing for no obvious reason, what should I do?&quot; may be too broad and open-ended for this format. It's better handled by a forum where people can have running discussions to rule out a series of tests. What do you guys think?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-29T01:30:44.290",
        "Id": "83",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-02-01T14:33:41.667",
        "OwnerUserId": "298",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "4",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;",
        "Title": "What about mystery-problem troubleshooting requests?",
        "ViewCount": "82"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "1",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/410/how-to-choose-a-right-3d-printer-filament-type&quot;&gt;How to choose a right 3D printer filament type?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I mean, this is usefull question. Why are you guys voting for close? It's not too broad, I formated it to be direct on topic.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thanks afterwards.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "1",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-28T09:13:04.087",
        "Id": "80",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-01-28T11:27:24.707",
        "LastEditDate": "2017-04-13T13:00:57.920",
        "LastEditorUserId": "-1",
        "OwnerUserId": "334",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "3",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;",
        "Title": "Why are you voting to close this question?",
        "ViewCount": "58"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AcceptedAnswerId": "82",
        "AnswerCount": "2",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;As you may or may not know, this is the third iteration of a proposal site that covers 3D Printing. The first 2 made it to the beta phase, but did not graduate  from the beta successfully:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://area51.stackexchange.com/proposals/41850/digital-fabrication&quot;&gt;Digital Fabrication&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://area51.stackexchange.com/proposals/22246/personal-manufacturing&quot;&gt;Personal Manufacturing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Would it be acceptable to extract &lt;code&gt;good&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;relevant&lt;/code&gt; questions out of these beta site question dumps and post them in the 3D Printing site?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-28T06:06:53.243",
        "Id": "79",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-01-29T15:06:59.207",
        "OwnerUserId": "150",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "3",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;&lt;site-promotion&gt;",
        "Title": "Questions from older beta sites",
        "ViewCount": "59"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "3",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;Questions like:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;x&lt;/em&gt; 3d printer is good?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;or&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;if it is my first printer, which model would you recommend&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;or&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;What printer model to buy?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;are on-topic?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I think if you ask&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I can not do &lt;em&gt;x&lt;/em&gt; with my 3d printer,  what printer to do &lt;em&gt;x&lt;/em&gt;?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Can be on-topic&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "1",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-27T22:27:25.883",
        "Id": "77",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-03-03T21:42:25.890",
        "OwnerUserId": "126",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "5",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;",
        "Title": "Discussions type: X 3d printer is good? are acceptable",
        "ViewCount": "58"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "7",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;When 3D Printing moves into public beta, you're going to want to get the word out. And fast! One of the best ways to advertise ourselves across the entire Stack Exchange network is through community ads. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;So what are these &quot;Community Ads?&quot;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Graduated sites allow the community to advertise relevant products or services within the site, using a system where the community chooses what to advertise. You can find these posts on per-site metas. Hint: these posts have the &lt;a href=&quot;/questions/tagged/community-ads&quot; class=&quot;post-tag moderator-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;community-ads&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;community-ads&lt;/a&gt; tag!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;Cool! What should the ad be like?&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There's a few requirements for these ads. Most notably,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;They must be 300px wide by 250px tall, or double for &quot;retina&quot; displays&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;There's a limit on file size of 150 kB.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The image must be hosted on i.stack.imgur (the Stack Exchange image hosting service).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Ads must be GIF or PNG (no animated GIFs).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h3&gt;What else should I know?&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To facilitate easy posting to other sites, make sure that the embedded image is of the following format:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;[![Tagline to show on mouseover][1]][2]&#xA;&#xA;   [1]: http://image-url&#xA;   [2]: http://clickthrough-url &#xA;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You can also include a message as a part of your answer with your own thoughts: why you chose some of the elements, and what sites the ads could potentially be posted to. Don't forget to critique each other as well!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Happy Designing!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "5",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-24T20:18:32.810",
        "Id": "76",
        "LastActivityDate": "2017-09-08T14:36:09.237",
        "OwnerUserId": "138",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "10",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;&lt;site-promotion&gt;",
        "Title": "Community Ads! Let's make 2d ads for ourselves!",
        "ViewCount": "260"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "3",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;We have only had activity on 3 questions in the past 2 days.  It is recommended that we get 10 new questions per day.  This is far below these goals.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What can we do to get more questions?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "1",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-24T12:36:52.690",
        "Id": "74",
        "LastActivityDate": "2017-06-07T20:10:34.897",
        "OwnerUserId": "43",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "13",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;",
        "Title": "How do we get more traffic to the site?",
        "ViewCount": "111"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "3",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;The questions so far are pretty strongly geared towards hobbyist/consumer FFF machines. That's not necessarily bad, since that's where most legit questions will come from. (Not much reason to ask questions about a plug-and-play industrial machine.) But it's a pretty important scope distinction. So far, askers are not really providing enough technology/make/model info to tell what kind of equipment they're running. An experienced expert can tell by context what the intention is, but that's not really scalable.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Sub-questions:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Will other AM technologies like SLA/DLP be included? If so, a pretty&#xA;rigorous clarification and tagging effort will be required to&#xA;separate out these other technologies.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Are industrial machines in scope? &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-20T19:59:36.883",
        "Id": "69",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-01-21T20:41:25.417",
        "OwnerUserId": "298",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "3",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;",
        "Title": "FFF/FDM vs... everything else?",
        "ViewCount": "123"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "1",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I just got a printer with swappable heads that can do FDM 3d printing, milling, and laser engraving. Presumably questions relating to the first are in scope here; how about the others? Or how about questions about the intersection? For example, a question about how best to design a model that can be produced &lt;em&gt;either&lt;/em&gt; by FDM or milling.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-19T01:48:12.217",
        "Id": "67",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-01-20T17:43:34.903",
        "OwnerUserId": "40",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "4",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;&lt;scope&gt;",
        "Title": "FDM printer that can also mill and engrave -- what's in scope?",
        "ViewCount": "95"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "3",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;We currently have quite a few tags about filament:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/filament&quot; class=&quot;post-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;filament&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;filament&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/plastic-filament&quot; class=&quot;post-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;plastic-filament&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;plastic-filament&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/thermoplastic-filament&quot; class=&quot;post-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;thermoplastic-filament&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;thermoplastic-filament&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;etc.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I feel like we need to clean these up and make clear what we'll use each tag for.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Thoughts?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "1",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-15T00:39:58.677",
        "Id": "59",
        "LastActivityDate": "2018-09-04T18:50:26.063",
        "OwnerUserId": "61",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "7",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;&lt;tags&gt;",
        "Title": "Fixing the filament tags",
        "ViewCount": "254"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "1",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;When asking my first question, I noticed we have a &quot;quality&quot; tag.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I used it to ask about the quality of the 3D printer in my question, but most other uses are about the quality of the prints.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Should we have separate tags, e.g. &quot;printer-quality&quot; and &quot;print-quality&quot;?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-01-13T20:12:22.463",
        "Id": "50",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-01-13T21:36:53.510",
        "OwnerUserId": "65",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "4",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;&lt;tags&gt;",
        "Title": "Should the &quot;quality&quot; tag be disambiguated?",
        "ViewCount": "44"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AcceptedAnswerId": "52",
        "AnswerCount": "6",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I believe this question is asked on every private Beta... what should be the name of our chatroom?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "2",
