        "AcceptedAnswerId": "606",
        "AnswerCount": "3",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I was checking tags and I saw that &amp;quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/slicer&quot;&gt;slicer&lt;/a&gt;&amp;quot; has only 6 questions, and no clear use case since there is already &amp;quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/slicing&quot;&gt;slicing&lt;/a&gt;&amp;quot;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There are some options now:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;reclassify those 6 questions into &amp;quot;slicing&amp;quot; and then set the two tags as synonyms&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;clarify the purpose of each tag which likely includes renaming them, because right now picking the correct one may not be obvious to most users. This may involve a general (re)classification into each tag of questions which were mistagged or not tagged with either one&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;",
