        "AnswerCount": "1",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I have a question about slicing. If I just describe the problem I would expect my question will be closed since the users have no way to reproduce the issue.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is there a way to share the stl file I'm using?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2024-01-24T04:46:21.827",
        "Id": "591",
        "LastActivityDate": "2024-01-24T12:20:42.687",
        "OwnerUserId": "21979",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "2",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;&lt;support&gt;",
        "Title": "How to share an stl file?",
        "ViewCount": "63"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "2",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I'm reviewing my recent suggested edits and don't understand why these five are rejected because:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The edit does not improve the quality of the post. Changes to the content are &lt;strong&gt;unnecessary or&lt;/strong&gt; make the post &lt;strong&gt;more confusing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17526&quot;&gt;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17526&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17532&quot;&gt;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17532&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17437&quot;&gt;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17437&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17435&quot;&gt;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17435&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17434&quot;&gt;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/review/suggested-edits/17434&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;None of the above examples contained a question in the title, and without reading anything else, one could not tell what the questioner would possibly try to ask or achieve. Each suggested edit clarifies the question's primary purpose a lot, making it &lt;em&gt;an improvement&lt;/em&gt; and certainly not &lt;em&gt;more confusing&lt;/em&gt;, for readers simply scrolling through the homepage and looking at the titles.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What can be improved to avoid future useless edits, which is a waste of time?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2023-11-27T13:11:16.877",
        "Id": "585",
        "LastActivityDate": "2023-11-27T22:09:22.380",
        "OwnerUserId": "36802",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "0",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;",
        "Title": "What is wrong with these suggested edits and why are they rejected?",
        "ViewCount": "62"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AcceptedAnswerId": "584",
        "AnswerCount": "3",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I'm dissapointed in the size of the active community on this site, considering how long the site has been active (&lt;a href=&quot;https://area51.stackexchange.com/proposals/82438/3d-printing&quot;&gt;https://area51.stackexchange.com/proposals/82438/3d-printing&lt;/a&gt;) and how mainstream 3D printing is. It's visible on the amount of views and votes that questions get, and the lack of answers on many questions. As well as a handful of users that are usually involved. It's unfortunate, I for example really like the (also relatively small) Information Security Stack site which is much more active.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I thought of ways to get people to even know about the existance of this site:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Posting links to this site on other sites such as when posting a make, or object on Thingiverse and Printables&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Using it more commonly in YouTube comments or other comments to link to answers or questions that are applicable in the context&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Question Migration from more popular sites such as StackOverflow, below are some examples of search queries that result in many (not all) questions that belong to this site instead:&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=3d+printing&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=3d+printing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=3d+print&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=3d+print&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=stl+obj&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=stl+obj&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=ender+3&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=ender+3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=klipper&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=klipper&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=gcode&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=gcode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=creality&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=creality&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=octoprint&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=octoprint&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=prusa&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=prusa&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=cura+slicer&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=cura+slicer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=marlin&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=marlin&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=bed+leveling&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=bed+leveling&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=pla+filament&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=pla+filament&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=print+filament&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=print+filament&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=thingiverse&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=thingiverse&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=grabcad&quot;&gt;https://stackoverflow.com/search?q=grabcad&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I think migration (also from other sites) is perhaps the most effective for multiple reasons. As I believe the user is notified, also more relevant content is available on this site making it easier found when using search engines. What are your thoughts on this, why isn't this community bigger and more active, did it used to be, what was already tried?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Also, not enough up and downvoting decreases the quality of this site a lot, since it's much harder to distinguish good quality from lower quality content.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "1",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2023-11-22T15:41:13.487",
        "Id": "582",
        "LastActivityDate": "2023-12-03T10:42:16.907",
        "OwnerUserId": "36802",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "0",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;",
        "Title": "Migrating questions to grow this site into a bigger and more active community?",
        "ViewCount": "71"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "1",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I don't have the needed reputation on this site yet and I didn't seen another option to suggest this, so I'm suggesting it here.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Please make the following tags one, as synonyms:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;input-shaping (the Marlin term)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;resonance-compensation (the Klipper term)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;vibration-compensation (the BambuLab term)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;They all describe the same concept to my understanding.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2023-11-21T13:08:04.830",
        "Id": "580",
        "LastActivityDate": "2023-11-21T22:49:50.167",
        "OwnerUserId": "36802",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "0",
        "Tags": "&lt;support&gt;&lt;tags&gt;&lt;tag-synonyms&gt;",
        "Title": "Merge input-shaping, resonance-compensation and vibration-compensation tags as synonyms",
        "ViewCount": "38"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AcceptedAnswerId": "578",
        "AnswerCount": "2",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;In addition to this: &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.meta.stackexchange.com/questions/428/is-photogrammetry-and-3d-scanning-on-topic&quot;&gt;Is photogrammetry and 3D scanning on-topic?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Shouldn't this site be called &amp;quot;3D manufacturing&amp;quot; or something broader? As 3D printing suggest only &amp;quot;printing&amp;quot; and not everything related to 3D printing such as 3D scanning or even 3D designing. I suppose that is off-topic? Is this scope defined somewhere?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Is everything related to (or for the purpose of) 3D printing such as 3D scanning using photogrammetry, NeRF or other techniques as well as 3D designing in-scope on this site?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I think both 3D scanning as well as 3D designing should be on-topic here.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2023-11-01T09:54:26.140",
        "Id": "577",
        "LastActivityDate": "2023-11-02T09:57:13.893",
        "OwnerUserId": "36802",
        "PostTypeId": "1",
        "Score": "0",
        "Tags": "&lt;discussion&gt;&lt;scope&gt;",
        "Title": "Is everything related to (or for the purpose of) 3D printing such as 3D scanning as well as 3D designing in-scope on this site?",
        "ViewCount": "36"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "AnswerCount": "1",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;Are questions that ask for a link to a specific type of model, STL file, or object file, such as this example, &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/q/20994/4762&quot;&gt;Where can I find an object file ir mesh file for a cilantro plant with thick exagerated cartoonish leaves?&lt;/a&gt;, on-topic?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;IMHO, whilst I am not against such questions, I feel that these types of questions are rather unlikely to be &lt;em&gt;particularly&lt;/em&gt; useful for other members of the community - they seem to have a &amp;quot;one-shot&amp;quot; type of appeal, which serve a unique set of circumstances that are unlikely to be encountered by others, or elsewhere - if that makes sense...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Usually the answer is &amp;quot;Look on Thingiverse (or a similar repository)&amp;quot;, or a link to a particular page on such a site.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Admittedly, these types of questions aren't very frequent and don't &lt;em&gt;really&lt;/em&gt; pose much of a problem (at the moment).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;What do people think?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr /&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If this is a duplicate, or a similar type of question has been asked previously, then kindly link to the meta question in the comments.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "1",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2023-06-19T09:28:41.463",
        "Id": "575",
        "LastActivityDate": "2023-12-27T00:01:10.227",
