      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;Your best bet?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;h1&gt;Start Community Ads!&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.meta.stackexchange.com/questions/76/community-ads-lets-make-2d-ads-for-ourselves&quot;&gt;Community Ads! Let&amp;#39;s make 2d ads for ourselves!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Community ads are served ads that you can display on any relevant site on the network! They are a great marketing tool, and makes your site known across the network, and attracts &lt;em&gt;experienced&lt;/em&gt; users that can help your site grow.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Also, make sure to keep your community. Encourage voting, good questions will be distinguished from your peers, and may even end up in the &lt;a href=&quot;https://stackexchange.com&quot;&gt;Hot Network Questions List&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-04-11T23:59:30.447",
        "Id": "122",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-04-11T23:59:30.447",
        "LastEditDate": "2017-03-16T16:43:51.887",
        "LastEditorUserId": "-1",
        "OwnerUserId": "138",
        "ParentId": "118",
        "PostTypeId": "2",
        "Score": "1"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;It seems like a great subject to incorporate, since bioprinting is 1) pretty neat and 2) an important application for 3D printing in general... but I sort of suspect none of our active users have the necessary expertise at the moment. It's a highly specialized field. We don't want the question to sit for an extended period with (at best) 1-2 mediocre answers, do we? That seems to be what happens to this sort of question at the site's current activity level. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "3",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
        "CreationDate": "2016-04-12T17:55:49.463",
        "Id": "124",
        "LastActivityDate": "2016-04-12T17:55:49.463",
        "OwnerUserId": "298",
        "ParentId": "123",
        "PostTypeId": "2",
        "Score": "3"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I think 3D bio printing - just like any kind of 3d printing - certainly should fall within the scope of this site. One could argue that such questions are hard to answer, and most likely outside the knowledge of most users, but I still think &lt;em&gt;good&lt;/em&gt; bio questions should be encouraged. &lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As for the linked question specifically, I think it is way too broad, asking not one, but perhaps five completely fine questions at the same time. Individually, I believe those questions would be answerable to the right person.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "2",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
