      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;99.9% sure this will be &lt;a href=&quot;/questions/tagged/status-declined&quot; class=&quot;post-tag moderator-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;status-declined&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;status-declined&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Issue is, we try to keep the UI clean. If you are truly interested in this, then you can look at the user's profile page. If you want to see what they are knowledgeable in, look at the top tags in their profile.  It just adds to much clutter to posts.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
