        "Body": "&lt;h1&gt;ERRORS&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Connecting 3D printed parts - For example, &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/6214/laser-engraver-with-smoothie-ramps-1-4-or-awc708c&quot;&gt;connecting 3D printed parts&lt;/a&gt; is currently off-topic&lt;sup&gt;2&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Coding - For example &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/3109/how-to-build-own-cura-gui&quot;&gt;How to build my own Cura GUI?&lt;/a&gt; - Coding Ultimaker Cura question, migrated to SO&lt;sup&gt;3&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;These two &amp;quot;footnotes&amp;quot; don't exist.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The first of the two does not seem to link to the question in the supposed title... in fact &lt;strong&gt;most&lt;/strong&gt; links seem to go... off sideways to the actual proper link. Might there be a numbering issue?!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
