      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "For questions about review warnings issued by moderators to users who have demonstrated a trend of incorrect review queue actions.",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2025-02-11T19:11:34.403",
        "Id": "616",
        "LastActivityDate": "2025-02-11T19:11:34.403",
        "LastEditDate": "2025-02-11T19:11:34.403",
        "LastEditorUserId": "-1",
        "OwnerUserId": "-1",
        "PostTypeId": "4",
        "Score": "0",
        "Title": "review-warning"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/scope&quot; class=&quot;post-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;scope&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;scope&lt;/a&gt; is used to define what is pertinent to discussion. Generally, the scope determines what the site is about. Issues arising from &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/scope&quot; class=&quot;post-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;scope&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;scope&lt;/a&gt; might have to do with whether a certain question is on-topic or not, but also can be used to evaluate whether an entire topic should be up for discussion (especially as it pertains to specific Stack Exchange sites).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Using this tag indicates that the question is requesting help with scope (normally as a specific use of a general topic), and answers should generally relate to the scope of the site and whether the topic raised generally relates. It also may be the case where a user has a question, but doesn't know where it belongs.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2018-10-15T06:41:19.163",
        "Id": "350",
        "LastActivityDate": "2018-10-23T13:07:53.447",
        "LastEditDate": "2018-10-23T13:07:53.447",
        "LastEditorUserId": "150",
        "OwnerUserId": "150",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;Discussion questions are the heart of your community.&#xA;For example: Should a certain question be allowed on the site? For what reason did a moderator lock a certain question? Are said actions setting a precedent?&#xA;Be sure to present your entire case and background information/data so the subject can be discussed fully.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2018-12-20T01:32:49.067",
        "Id": "376",
        "LastActivityDate": "2019-02-07T03:49:35.347",
        "LastEditDate": "2019-02-07T03:49:35.347",
        "LastEditorUserId": "13890",
        "OwnerUserId": "13890",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;This tag is used by staff when sharing concepts in the Discovery phase relating to product or configuration changes. In most cases a direction and/or goal has been established, and there has likely been some amount of time invested into discovery work and research. The post is being presented to the Community for feedback to be taken into consideration. Where possible, the post includes specific questions to help guide Community feedback.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2020-04-24T13:33:15.850",
        "Id": "486",
        "LastActivityDate": "2020-04-27T18:21:31.377",
        "LastEditDate": "2020-04-27T18:21:31.377",
        "LastEditorUserId": "-1",
        "OwnerUserId": "-1",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;A feature request or bug report with this tag is neither declined nor destined for implementation/fix. When such a decision has been made, the tag will be changed accordingly.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There are multiple factors that may leave a report under review. There could be consideration of whether the proposed feature or bugfix is feasible or useful. There could be investigations on the complexity of the necessary solution. There could be insufficient information in the feature or bug report as presented. Site developers may provide additional comments to request more information or to provide status updates as appropriate to the status of the review, until such time as the decision for approval or decline is made.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Status tags can only be applied by staff and ♦ moderators; the latter will only use this tag as part of the escalation process described here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://meta.stackexchange.com/q/348642/295232&quot;&gt;What posts should be escalated to staff using [status-review], and how do I escalate them?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;sub&gt;Copied from: &lt;a href=&quot;https://meta.stackexchange.com/tags/status-review/info&quot;&gt;https://meta.stackexchange.com/tags/status-review/info&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2020-07-26T12:17:30.317",
        "Id": "492",
        "LastActivityDate": "2020-09-13T19:23:41.163",
        "LastEditDate": "2020-09-13T19:23:41.163",
        "LastEditorUserId": "4808",
        "OwnerUserId": "4808",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;A feature request or bug with this tag is something that has been evaluated as positive on potential,&#xA;but it is not present in the current work timeline. It is also not guaranteed to be implemented - when&#xA;it resurfaces the proposal may be re-evaluated and declined depending on how the situation has changed since then.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Contrast &lt;a href=&quot;/questions/tagged/status-planned&quot; class=&quot;post-tag moderator-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;status-planned&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;status-planned&lt;/a&gt;, in which a feature is something that the site developers have&#xA;definitively approved for implementation but the timing is unknown.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Status tags can only be applied by moderators and site developers.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2022-05-30T12:37:46.333",
        "Id": "538",
        "LastActivityDate": "2022-06-01T13:50:40.447",
        "LastEditDate": "2022-06-01T13:50:40.447",
        "LastEditorUserId": "5456",
        "OwnerUserId": "5456",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;A feature request or bug with this tag is something that has been evaluated as definitive to implementation.&#xA;However, either there is ongoing investigation on the methods to implement the proposal, or there are other&#xA;active projects that are ahead of it in priority for the site developers. Ideally, this tag indicates that&#xA;the proposal is intended to be implemented in the near term.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Contrast &lt;a href=&quot;/questions/tagged/status-deferred&quot; class=&quot;post-tag moderator-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;status-deferred&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;status-deferred&lt;/a&gt;, in which the feature is of lower priority and may be re-evaluated&#xA;on feasibility at a later date.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Status tags can only be applied by moderators and site developers.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2022-05-30T12:40:06.693",
        "Id": "540",
        "LastActivityDate": "2022-06-01T13:51:29.203",
        "LastEditDate": "2022-06-01T13:51:29.203",
        "LastEditorUserId": "5456",
        "OwnerUserId": "5456",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;Before posting your question, please check the &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.meta.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/faq&quot;&gt;FAQs&lt;/a&gt;, and do a &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.meta.stackexchange.com/search&quot;&gt;search&lt;/a&gt; to see if your problem already has a known solution or procedure. If you cannot find an answer, we will be happy to help you.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2022-05-30T12:41:26.287",
        "Id": "542",
        "LastActivityDate": "2022-06-01T13:51:21.357",
        "LastEditDate": "2022-06-01T13:51:21.357",
        "LastEditorUserId": "5456",
        "OwnerUserId": "5456",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;A bug report is considered not reproducible if it is a bug that the site developers&#xA;would fix, but cannot due to an inability to recreate the problematic behavior in&#xA;spite of attempts to do so. Reports that are not reproducible typically represent&#xA;bugs that come from using unsupported browsers and tools, or because of sunspots&#xA;and other activity entirely unrelated to the site creating a momentary issue.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If a bug can’t be reproduced due to being immediately presented as being through&#xA;an unsupported browser, thus bypassing the need of the site developers to even&#xA;attempt to reproduce the bug, then &lt;a href=&quot;/questions/tagged/status-declined&quot; class=&quot;post-tag moderator-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;status-declined&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;status-declined&lt;/a&gt; should be used.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;If you are the reporter of a bug that receives this tag, it may indicate&#xA;that the bug was intermittent, or merely that you didn't thoroughly explain&#xA;the circumstances under which you encountered it. First, verify that &lt;em&gt;you&lt;/em&gt;&#xA;can still cause the bug to appear, and (if you can) then:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Describe in detail what you were doing when it happened. Include links to any relevant pages / posts.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;List the steps you took to encounter the bug.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Describe your environment: browser make and version, OS, add-ons, userscripts (if applicable).&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Include screenshots if applicable. Use hand-drawn circles to highlight key portions&#xA;of the problem.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Status tags can only be applied by moderators and site developers.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2022-06-01T14:35:07.957",
        "Id": "544",
        "LastActivityDate": "2022-06-02T22:15:45.803",
        "LastEditDate": "2022-06-02T22:15:45.803",
        "LastEditorUserId": "5456",
        "OwnerUserId": "5456",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;Note that some printer variants are vastly different from their core machine.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A Prusa i3 and its Mark 2, 2S, 3, 2.5, 4 and 4S renditions have differences that make some things inaplicable to earlier renditions, especially with the motherboards changing, finer stepper motors... the most hard cut was the 4, which in some parts was so different, that earlier versions could not be sensibly upgraded in some regards.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Among the Ender 3 series, there's the v3, including SE and KE. The most noticable differences is the lack of bed leveling knobs and direct drive extruder, making them behave &lt;strong&gt;vastly&lt;/strong&gt; different in bed leveling to the normal ender3, and profiles are not easily transferable...&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;version or mark number&lt;/strong&gt; would be at least appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2025-04-14T02:52:28.113",
        "Id": "620",
        "LastActivityDate": "2025-04-14T02:52:28.113",
        "OwnerUserId": "8884",
        "ParentId": "618",
        "PostTypeId": "2",
        "Score": "1"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;I was the one that added the tag for that printer. I did so because there are some differences between it and most of the generic Ender 3 line of printers, such as a different chassis and Y-axis design, the newer Slicer direct-drive extruder, and supports higher print speeds than most of the others, which means that settings for filaments (temp, print speed, retraction distance and speed) will differ from most of those generic models.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I think the differences between it and the generic Ender 3 line are significant enough to warrant a separate tag, just as you thought the P3Steel was different enough from the generic Prusa printers to need a separate tag in &lt;a href=&quot;https://3dprinting.meta.stackexchange.com/a/287/43303&quot;&gt;Tagging for printer specific brand and type&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A few of those features are shared with the Ender 3 v3 KE, although it differs in having linear rods instead of linear rails for the Y-axis, a textured PEI build plate, and nearly double the rated max print speed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I certainly found significant differences between the old Ender 3 I have and the new Ender 3 v3 KE that I bought, and found I couldn't use any of my existing printer or filament profiles on the KE without losing functionality in part. Even if I didn't take advantage of it having Klipper instead of Marlin and just stuck with Marlin-style gcode, I wouldn't have been able to get functionality out of the older profiles.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "3",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2025-03-09T14:41:29.150",
        "Id": "619",
        "LastActivityDate": "2025-03-09T14:41:29.150",
        "OwnerUserId": "43303",
        "ParentId": "618",
        "PostTypeId": "2",
        "Score": "3"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;A bug report is considered reproduced only if the site developers have successfully reproduced the bug.&#xA;This tag should only be applied if the site developers cannot immediately address the bug, such as if&#xA;it requires further investigation into solutions or if the implementation of a fix would be stalled&#xA;for other reasons. When a fix is eventually implemented, the tag should become &lt;a href=&quot;/questions/tagged/status-completed&quot; class=&quot;post-tag moderator-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;status-completed&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;status-completed&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Status tags can only be applied by moderators and site developers.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2022-06-01T14:35:38.467",
        "Id": "546",
        "LastActivityDate": "2022-06-02T22:15:56.530",
        "LastEditDate": "2022-06-02T22:15:56.530",
        "LastEditorUserId": "5456",
        "OwnerUserId": "5456",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;A bug report is considered bydesign if, after review of the detailed erroneous behavior,&#xA;it is determined that the behavior is desirable to keep in place rather than fix. This&#xA;is independent of whether or not the behavior was formerly known to the site developers&#xA;prior to the time of the report - the important thing is that the behavior will not be&#xA;altered because its current behavior is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This tag should only be used on questions reporting what is purported as erroneous behavior&#xA;and suggests them being fixed / reversed. For when a question that is requesting a new&#xA;feature that addresses a behavior that the asker believes to be erroneous,&#xA;&lt;a href=&quot;/questions/tagged/status-declined&quot; class=&quot;post-tag moderator-tag&quot; title=&quot;show questions tagged &amp;#39;status-declined&amp;#39;&quot; rel=&quot;tag&quot;&gt;status-declined&lt;/a&gt; should be used.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Status tags can only be applied by moderators and site developers.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2022-06-01T14:36:09.787",
        "Id": "548",
        "LastActivityDate": "2022-06-02T22:15:27.087",
        "LastEditDate": "2022-06-02T22:15:27.087",
        "LastEditorUserId": "5456",
        "OwnerUserId": "5456",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      },
      {
        "": "row",
        "-": "posts",
        "--": null,
        "@index": 0,
        "@tail": null,
        "@text": "",
        "Body": "&lt;p&gt;See the &lt;a href=&quot;/help/review-warnings&quot;&gt;help center&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;",
        "CommentCount": "0",
        "ContentLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "CreationDate": "2025-02-11T19:11:34.403",
        "Id": "615",
        "LastActivityDate": "2025-02-11T19:11:34.403",
        "LastEditDate": "2025-02-11T19:11:34.403",
        "LastEditorUserId": "-1",
        "OwnerUserId": "-1",
        "PostTypeId": "5",
        "Score": "0"
      }
    ]
